.TH VALIDATE-GSDB-INTENSIVE-REVIEW 1 "2026-09-06" "TinyCalc" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
validate-gsdb-intensive-review \- read-only validation of the TinyCalc GSDB assessment
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B validate-gsdb-intensive-review.sh
[\fB--action\fR ACTION] [\fB--assessment\fR FILE] [\fB--repository-root\fR DIR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The command validates the Feature 005 evidence matrix without changing files.
The Bash 3 compatible entry delegates to the PowerShell 7 semantic engine.
Die deutsche und englische Bedienhilfe ist auch über PowerShell Get-Help und
die Option --help verfügbar.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --action ACTION
Select Validate, ValidateFixtures, ValidateSources, ValidateCompendium, or
ValidateMappings. Hyphenated lower-case forms are accepted by the Bash entry.
.TP
.B --assessment FILE
Select the assessment JSON file. The default is the Feature 005 production
matrix.
.TP
.B --repository-root DIR
Select the repository root used for source and evidence resolution.
.TP
.B -h, --help
Show bilingual compact help.
.SH READ-ONLY BOUNDARY
The validator reads JSON, Markdown, source manifests, and repository evidence.
It does not modify the assessment, source files, Git index, provider state, or
secrets. A dry-run switch is therefore not applicable while this boundary
remains true.
.SH FAILURE CLASSES
GSDB001 covers missing or invalid UTF-8/JSON/schema input. GSDB002 covers source
binding and safe-path failures. GSDB003 covers canonical ID failures. GSDB004
covers compendium parity. GSDB005 covers assessment fields and status axes.
GSDB006 covers unsupported positive evidence. GSDB007 covers Human-only or
approval boundaries. GSDB008 covers duty, preset, workflow, or validator
coverage. GSDB009 covers finding linkage. GSDB010 covers summary, ordering,
date, or hash drift.
Preset mappings and finding links are checked as exact reciprocal sets.
Generic evidence locators and unbound evidence paths are rejected. Invalid
actions and options are reported without echoing their supplied values.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Zero means the selected contract passed. One means validation failed and stderr
begins with exactly one stable GSDB failure class.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
bash scripts/validate-gsdb-intensive-review.sh --action validate \
  --assessment docs/security/gsdb-intensive-review/evidence-matrix.json \
  --repository-root .

pwsh -NoProfile -File scripts/validate-gsdb-intensive-review.ps1 \
  -Action ValidateFixtures -RepositoryRoot .
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
docs/security/gsdb-intensive-review/evidence-matrix.md and
specs/005-gsdb-intensive-review/checklists/script-parity.md provide the complete
bilingual assessment and parity evidence.
